{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkCdcHMcz7v7uYhbS2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, `this.getQueue()` is synchronous. The Cloudflare docs say \"This method is synchronous,\" and it returns the item directly instead of a Promise:\n\n```ts\ngetQueue<T>(id: string): QueueItem<T> | undefined\n```\n\nYou don't need `await`. It returns `undefined` if no queued task has that ID.\n\n**`QueueItem<T>` fields:**\n\n| Field | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `string` | ID of the queued task |\n| `payload` | `T` | Data that will be passed to the callback |\n| `callback` | `keyof Agent` | Name of the agent method that will be called |\n| `created_at` | `number` | When the task was queued |\n| `retry` | optional | Retry options for this task |\n\n```ts\nconst item = this.getQueue<{ userId: string }>(taskId);\nif (item) {\n  console.log(item.callback, item.payload.userId, item.created_at);\n}\n```\n\nThe Ludion knowledge base had nothing on this, so this answer comes only from the official docs page.\n\nSources:\n- [Cloudflare Agents – Queue tasks](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/queue-tasks/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":4550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ff595ac-be2c-4329-96ac-bbe0521130a9","uuid":"c9bc35fe-733d-4f20-8a93-6fca779d93ec","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:09:57.346Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkCdJR6nWETZCHsAYd7"}
